# SPA fallback — Netlify / Cloudflare Pages.
#
# Routing is client-side, so the server has no file at /difference, /invest and
# so on. Without this rule a visitor who types a deep link, follows one from
# search, or refreshes anywhere other than the home page gets a 404.
#
# Real files on disk always win over this rule, so /config.json, /images/*,
# /video/*, /sitemap.xml and /robots.txt are still served normally.
#
# 200 rather than 301: the URL must stay as the visitor typed it, otherwise the
# router never sees the route it is meant to render.
/*  /index.html  200
